---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { isPreview } from '../../lib/deployment';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Info"
  description="About Alkemist, the Astro toolkit for inventors and researchers."
  preview={isPreview}
>
  <article class="alk-prose">
    <h1>About Alkemist</h1>
    <p class="alk-lead">
      An Astro toolkit for technical writing, charts, and interactive models.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use it for a personal notebook, a research group, or an independent
      project.
    </p>
    <h2>Customization</h2>
    <p>
      Your content, identity, and page layouts belong to your site. Shared
      components and defaults live in packages you can update. The <a
        href="/docs/getting-started/">starter</a
      > creates a separate project with its own configuration and content.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses the components it documents. The <a href="/blog/">blog</a> records
      the work, <a href="/labs/">Labs</a> holds interactive experiments, and the <a
        href="/docs/">docs</a
      > explain how to use the toolkit.
    </p>
    <h2>Project status</h2>
    <p>
      Alkemist is public source. The documented API is available from the source
      checkout, with its next npm release pending. See <a href="/docs/status/"
        >what is available and what is planned</a
      >.
    </p>
    <div class="alk-links">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started →</a><a
        href="/docs/components/">Browse the components →</a
      >
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
